  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through next Thursday) \nIssued at 1040 PM CDT Thu Oct 29 2026\n\nSome model guidance is still showing some lingering precipitation\noff the caprock through Saturday morning. However, this is most \nlikely low stratus and possibly drizzle. Short wave ridging will \nreturn late Saturday through the day on Sunday in advance of the \nnext trough digging into the western CONUS. The next short wave \ntrough will track to the four corners by Monday morning providing \nanother shot of precipitation from late Sunday through Monday. \nForcing associated with this short wave looks to be briefer than \nwhat is expected for Friday but also may be stronger. The other \nnotable feature in the long term forecast will be a strong cold \nfront currently forecast to move through on Tuesday morning. \nSurface winds will pack a punch behind this front but temperatures\ndon't appear to be significantly affected.",
